    "title": "Offset, Former Migos Rapper, Is Shot Outside Florida Casino",
    "text": "AdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENTThe former member of the Atlanta trio was in stable condition after being shot in Hollywood, Fla., his representative said. Another rapper, Lil Tjay, was charged with disorderly conduct.The rapper Offset was injured in a shooting in Hollywood, Fla., on Monday.Credit...Peyton Fulford for The New York TimesApril 6, 2026The rapper Offset was injured in a shooting on Monday evening outside a casino in Hollywood, Fla., his representative said.The Seminole Police Department said in a statement that a shooting, which had started as a fight, occurred after 7 p.m. in the valet area of the Seminole Hard Rock Hotel and Casino.The police did not name Offset, but Nathalie Moar, a spokeswoman for the rapper, said he was the injured person. As of Tuesday morning, Offset, 34, remained in a hospital in stable condition with a non-life-threatening injury, according to Gary Bitner, a spokesman for the Seminole Police Department.Subscribe to The Times to read as many articles as you like.Claire Moses is a Times reporter in London, focused on coverage of breaking and trending news.A version of this article appears in print on April 8, 2026, Section C, Page 4 of the New York edition with the headline: The Rapper Offset Was Shot at a Casino. Order Reprints | Today’s Paper | SubscribeRelated ContentAdvertisementSKIP ADVERTISEMENT",
